description:
FILED s518e (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-17), found while probing the Type-Tiny census (Type::Library idiom `sort $lib->meta->type_names` family).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs main ff4c1500 and s518e):

    package K; sub new { bless {}, shift } sub names { ("b", "a") }
    package main;
    print join(",", sort K->new->names), "\n";

perl: `a,b`.  PCL: "PCL: statement not supported ... -- WTF? :-) Expr starts with ->/brace??" (statement dropped / dies in eval).  perl reads `sort WORD->...` as sort LIST where the bareword is a class (the `->` rules out SUBNAME).  NOT FIXED (PExpr sort-operand parse, the #153 region -- needs a design look).


=== DONE (s520a, Opus 5.5, 2026-10-18) ===
Commit b662471e.  NOT in the `$end_pars` region: ONE predicate `_sort_word_is_subname` (Pl/PExpr.pm) for sort's first word, bare and parenthesised (the two copies of the keyword test folded): a WORD followed by `->` is a CLASS starting the LIST.  Probes p5/ = perl: `sort K->new->names`, `sort(K->new->names)`, `sort { $b cmp $a } K->new->names`, `sort foo @l` (declared sub stays SUBNAME), `sort $ref @l`, `sort Foo::bar @l`, `reverse K->new->names`.  Guard Pl/t/sort-01.t row 24 (inverse FAIL).  ir-spec §5.4.  Batch bars: session-log ## Session s520a.
